Subject: [PATCH] panvk: declare v9 per-arch prototypes in panvk_physical_device.c

STATUS: HISTORICAL / ILLUSTRATIVE - does not apply to the base commit.

The ---/+++ paths are bare filenames ("panvk_physical_device.c") rather than
"a/"-prefixed repo-relative paths, so `git apply` from the repo root cannot
locate the target. The real file is
src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c, and at base commit
6598829019c0746aa8e473b4ae1c980cbfa6ea4b the PER_ARCH_FUNCS block starts at
line 75, not 73.

Kept because it isolates one specific bug: PER_ARCH_FUNCS is a macro generator
invoked manually per arch, and 9 was simply missing from the list, so
libpanvk_v9.a compiled while panvk_physical_device.c failed with
implicit-function-declaration. **The applicable patch is
0014-panvk-v9-arch-enablement-common.patch**, which adds PER_ARCH_FUNCS(9)
against the correct base.

--- panvk_physical_device.c.pre-v9-proto	2026-09-09
+++ panvk_physical_device.c	2026-09-09
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
 
 PER_ARCH_FUNCS(6);
 PER_ARCH_FUNCS(7);
+PER_ARCH_FUNCS(9);
 PER_ARCH_FUNCS(10);
 PER_ARCH_FUNCS(12);
 PER_ARCH_FUNCS(13);
